# CSS Formatting

Write each selector as an expanded block. Put the opening `{` on the same line as the selector, one declaration per line, and indent declarations with **2 spaces**.

```css
/* ❌ BAD — compacted single-line rules */
.recent-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--sp-3);padding:14px;}
.rr-note{font-weight:600;font-size:14px;}

/* ✅ GOOD — expanded multi-line rules */
.recent-row {
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  gap: var(--sp-3);
  padding: 14px;
}

.rr-note {
  font-weight: 600;
  font-size: 14px;
}
```

## Details

- Space before `{` and after `:` (`display: flex`, not `display:flex`)
- Trailing semicolon on every declaration
- Blank line between top-level rule blocks
- Keep related selectors grouped; prefer separate blocks over long comma-chained one-liners when editing
- When changing existing compacted CSS, expand the rules you touch into this form
